# Feed-validation test suite cases.
#
# One case per line, pipe-separated:
#
#   name | packages | expected-libs | boot | assertions
#
#   name           short case id (used for the per-case project dir)
#   packages       space-separated feed package names to install (empty for boot-only)
#   expected-libs  space-separated shared-lib basenames to assert (optional)
#   boot           "yes" to also run the boot e2e (heavy: one image cycle), else "no"
#   assertions     named assertion set for the boot tier (default: ext+libs check)
#                  "luks-var" -> fvl_assert_luks_var (checks dm-crypt /var active)
#
# Adding a test = adding a line. Names are the real feed package names
# (e.g. zeromq, not libzmq - debian renaming is not active here).
#
# name              | packages               | expected-libs | boot | assertions
zeromq              | zeromq                 | libzmq.so.5   | yes  |
# Boot-only cases: no feed package to install, the assertion set is the test.
luks-var            |                        |               | yes  | luks-var
# One representative package per feature group, so a group that stops
# producing anything fails here rather than silently shipping an empty feed.
# The visual groups also run the boot e2e; the rest assert feed presence only.
#
# No cameras or cloud-aws case: meta-basler-tools, meta-intel-realsense and
# meta-aws have no wrynose branch, so those groups cannot be selected here yet.
# Add the case in the same commit that adds the layer back.
system-base         | vim                    |               | no   |
networking          | networkmanager         |               | no   |
multimedia          | gstreamer1.0           |               | no   |
python              | python3-pip            |               | no   |
graphics            | weston                 |               | yes  |
qt                  | qtbase                 |               | yes  |
browsers            | chromium-ozone-wayland |               | yes  |
ai                  | dx-driver              |               | no   |
java                | openjdk-17-jre         |               | no   |
containers          | podman                 |               | no   |
